# PropFlow design rule

The design package lives in `design/` (adjust the path if you put it elsewhere).
It is the source of truth for every UI decision. Read `design/DESIGN.md` before building or changing a screen.

## Before building a screen
1. Find the screen in DESIGN.md §6 (screen ↔ route map) and open its mockup in `design/screens/<role>/<Name>.dc.html`.
2. Read the `renderVals()` block at the bottom of the mockup. Its return value is the data/props shape for the component.
3. Rebuild the markup 1:1: same order, same spacing, same sizes, same Thai copy (character for character).

## Translating `.dc.html` to React + Tailwind
- `<x-dc>` content = the component JSX. Ignore `<helmet>`, `support.js`, `data-props`.
- `{{value}}` → prop or derived value. `<sc-for list="{{items}}" as="item">` → `items.map(...)` with a stable `key`.
- `<sc-if value="{{x}}">` → `{x && ...}`.
- `<dc-import name="TabBar" .../>` → shared component. Sources are in `design/screens/components/`.
- `<a href="X.dc.html">` → router link to the route of X (DESIGN.md §6).
- Inline styles → Tailwind classes from the preset in `design/tokens/tailwind.config.js`. Arbitrary values (`p-[14px]`) are fine for one-off px values; arbitrary colors are not.

## Hard rules
- Colors only from tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted`, `bg-warn-bg text-warn-fg`, ...). No other hex values.
- `brand` (#06C755) is never a background behind white text. Use `primary` (#047C3B) for buttons.
- Fonts: `font-display` (Anuphan) for headings and amounts, `font-sans` (Sarabun) for everything else. Amounts use `.pf-amount` / `tabular-nums`.
- Status = color + Thai word, always via one `<StatusBadge kind status />` that reads `design/tokens/tokens.json` → `statusMap`. Never color alone.
- Mobile (LIFF): design width 390, min 360, `max-w-liff mx-auto`. Primary action in a sticky bottom action bar, buttons 52px high, tap targets ≥ 44px.
- Portal (desktop): sidebar + main as in the mockups (flex-wrap, sidebar `1 1 240px`, main `999 1 560px`). Buttons 44px.
- Icons: lucide-react, 20–24px, stroke 2, matching the mockup icon names.
- Build shared components first (DESIGN.md §4) and reuse them. Do not restyle a component per screen.
- Loading = skeletons, empty = one muted line + one primary action, errors inline. Follow DESIGN.md §8.
- Items in DESIGN.md §7 need backend work. Build the UI, but put mock data behind a clear TODO if the API does not exist yet.
- Values shown as `[ราคา]`, `[ยอด]` etc. in mockups are placeholders: read them from config/API, never hard-code.
